<title>USA: Fla. 350 MW McIntosh coal unit back up - sources.</title>
<headline>Fla. 350 MW McIntosh coal unit back up - sources.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>A 350 megawatt (MW) coal-fired unit at the McIntosh generating station returned to operation early Thursday after being shut Saturday to repair a boiler tube leak, sources familiar with the operation said.</p>
<p>The unit, called McIntosh 3, is jointly owned by the cities of Lakeland (60 percent) and Orlando (40). It is located in Lakeland, Fla.</p>
<p>Two natural-gas fired units at the McIntosh facility, with combined capacity of 200 MW, were operating normally, sources said.</p>
<p>--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1622</p>
